# q2352–q2353: disclosure time and provenance

The selected clock producer initializes a missing world-clock row before its
explicit missing-row error. Disclosure would use minute zero if that error were
returned, but no ordinary supported error witness is established.

A same-case disclosure accepts an invalid outer-None provenance result, while
observer and action lookups require an outer Some. Valid manual Some(None) is
distinct. Selected manual and generated authoring paths provide safeguards; the
reachability of invalid provenance through supported callers remains open.

REPORT.json retains the original 059 and older 774 attribution, current source
references, ledger relationships, bounded thirteen-lens perspectives and
remaining questions. READ-LIMITS.json distinguishes actual source displays from
unread captures. No product execution or validation occurred.
